like, training for those validation steps.

00:45:16.584 --> 00:45:22.063
Like I… So the boss or whoever says,
"Great, this is great. Let's assign

00:45:22.064 --> 00:45:26.892
this person," is there anywhere that
you know to go to sort of help with

00:45:26.952 --> 00:45:28.741
implementing something like this?

00:45:28.814 --> 00:45:33.055
Um, or is it sort of… I, I haven't heard
of this sort of concept, so it sort of

00:45:33.056 --> 00:45:35.055
sounds like maybe this is new territory.

00:45:35.831 --> 00:45:38.225
Yeah, I think this is
pretty new, at least to me.

00:45:38.259 --> 00:45:41.914
Uh, unfortunately I don't have resources
yet, but the question immediately pinged

00:45:41.914 --> 00:45:45.510
in my mind, hmm, I should make this
kind of content available for people.

00:45:45.812 --> 00:45:50.285
So I will look into that, so stay
tuned for that- Perfect … at least

00:45:50.285 --> 00:45:51.888
then, at least I will have something.

00:45:52.341 --> 00:45:55.982
But yeah, it's, it's a bit tricky
because, of course, all of these are so

00:45:55.982 --> 00:46:00.073
different based on the task we are doing
and the type of organization in place.

00:46:00.081 --> 00:46:04.194
So I understand why there aren't
